* A way to walk out of the boardwalk pool in the far west (openc2e Creatures
* 2 project, our own script). Run by openc2e after the world loads
* (Additions folder); safe to repeat. ROOM takes all of a room's data, so
* each room's own values are passed back.
*
* The pool (room 110, water, x 669-1091) lies under the boardwalk (room 109,
* deck line y 1319). Its walls were solid, the boardwalk's west end opened
* straight down into it (room 111, the air over the pool's west end), and
* creatures cannot climb up, so a creature that fell in stayed (owner,
* 2026-11-10: a trapped norn). The picture already has the way out: at the
* pool's east end an earth bank rises out of the water (from about y 1400 at
* x 1080 to 1333 at x 1223) and the boardwalk's east part rests on it. The
* rooms now follow it:
* - the pool reaches x 1170, its floor along the painted bed and up the bank
*   to the water's surface (y 1352) at x 1170;
* - the boardwalk's east part (x 1170-1342) becomes its own room (113, until
*   now the sealed pipe chamber under the bank): its floor line starts at
*   the water's surface where the bank leaves the pool (x 1170, y 1352),
*   follows the painted bank up to 1333 at x 1223, meets the deck at 1319
*   by x 1250, and goes on east to room 108 as before. (It first met the
*   bank as a 33 px step, which creatures cannot climb: a frog norn starved
*   at its foot, owner 2026-11-11.)
* - the pipe chamber (with its small lift, 3 2 4) is all of room 112 now,
*   x 1091-1473 below y 1440;
* - the boardwalk's west end is a wall: nothing walks off it into the pool
*   (room 111 stays as the air over the water, where the fish leap).
